{"repositoryId":1415483739,"availability":"available","full":"mr-finster/miyoo64","name":"miyoo64","description":"N64 games for the Miyoo Mini, built from the decomp projects. Bring your own ROM.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":19,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-12T11:14:49Z","updated":"2026-10-18T12:15:09Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://miyoo-n64.pages.dev","topics":["decompilation","miyoo-mini","n64"],"demo":"https://miyoo-n64.pages.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.561Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.561Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.561Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T04:16:31.458Z","stars":4,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.561Z","stars":19,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ten N64 games running natively on the Miyoo Mini family, built from the decompilation projects.","No ROMs or game data are included, here or in the downloads. Bring your own ROM: each game reads a copy of a game you own and builds what it needs on the Miyoo itself.","Native ports of ten N64 games to the Miyoo Mini family (Mini, Mini Plus, Mini v4, Mini Flip). No emulation: each game's C code, rebuilt by its decompilation community, runs on the Mini's ARM CPU and is drawn by a software renderer that uses both of its cores. Every game has save states (9 slots and an auto save), the same in-game menu (MENU: resume, save, load, exit), and picks up where you left off after a power-off."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mr-finster/miyoo64/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3b5b061d0df6b8a566b3d1e70ffc40b0a46384d57fe81aab46b1f436765cc6e4","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.633Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:56:33.633Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ten N64 games running natively on the Miyoo Mini family, built from the decompilation projects.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mr-finster/miyoo64/blob/main/README.m